# .pubignore REPLACES .gitignore for `dart pub publish`.
#
# It exists so the DevTools extension bundle SHIPS. The root .gitignore excludes
# packages/*/extension/devtools/build/ (37MB of canvaskit has no business in git
# history), but pub archives git-tracked files by default — so the bundle was
# simply absent from the archive and pub rejected the package:
#
#   It looks like you are making a devtools extension!
#   The folder `extension/devtools` should contain both a `config.yaml` file
#   and a non-empty `build` directory
#
# Because this file takes precedence over .gitignore, the build/ directory is
# included in the published archive while staying untracked in git. Re-run
# tool/build_devtools_extension.sh before publishing so the shipped bundle is
# current — it is a build artifact, not a source of truth.
#
# Everything below mirrors the root .gitignore EXCEPT the devtools build.
.dart_tool/
build/
!extension/devtools/build/
.packages
pubspec.lock
